-- title:
--   The literal quotient conic parameter gives a cubic extension of actual function fields
-- statement:
--   Over every characteristic-zero field, the original conic field equals the field generated by the rational slope parameter; adjoining the original x coordinate gives the actual full curve field, with its original explicit monic cubic, integral root and degree bound three. Fifteen full original types, both field and polynomial data values and eight original scalar algebra providers are compared. Named downstream consumer: the exact rational order-three diamond fixed field.
-- source:
--   Complete original MazurTheorem Order13FieldConicFieldCubicExtension using published actual general-field conic parametrization and coordinate field generators. Official Anthropic FLT interfaces at 6e837e75355538c7f80bab5b956861e86c4eacc2, Apache-2.0.

